T:------------
T:What it is
T:Data is a
T:collection
T:of discrete
T:or
T:continuous
T:values that
T:conveys
T:facts,
T:describing
T:the
T:quantity,
T:quality,
T:fact,
T:statistics,
T:other basic
T:units of
T:meaning, or
T:simply
T:sequences of
T:symbols that
T:may be
T:further
T:interpreted
T:formally. A
T:datum, data
T:value or
T:data point
T:is an
T:individual
T:value in a
T:collection
T:of data.
T:Data is
T:usually
T:organized
T:into
T:structures
T:such as
T:tables that
T:provide
T:additional
T:context and
T:meaning, and
T:may itself
T:be used as
T:data in
T:larger
T:structures.
T:Data may be
T:used as
T:variables in
T:a
T:computationa
T:process.
T:Data may
T:represent
T:abstract
T:ideas or
T:concrete
T:measurement.
T:Data is
T:commonly
T:used in
T:scientific
T:research,
T:economics,
T:and
T:virtually
T:every other
T:form of
T:human
T:organization
T:activity.
T:Examples of
T:data sets
T:include
T:price
T:indices,
T:unemployment
T:rates,
T:literacy
T:rates, and
T:census data.
T:In this
T:context,
T:data
T:represents
T:the raw
T:facts and
T:figures from
T:which useful
T:facts can be
T:extracted.
